From 000851915590fb7990c4a5e203f080955eeb71b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:55:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AdaptiveLinearSolverTolerance: review (safeguard of the first
 choice, tests)

- Safeguard of the first choice of Eisenstat and Walker: eta^((1+sqrt(5))/2),
  independent of Gamma and Alpha, as in their paper and in PETSc (MFEM uses
  gamma eta^alpha for both choices; the values only differ with other
  values of Gamma and Alpha than the default ones).
- The default initial tolerance is bounded by the maximum one: a maximum
  tolerance below 0.5 may be given alone.
- Documentation: the tolerance may be lower than the one of the linear
  solver; residual of the complete linear solve after a reduction of the
  correction; glossary section on the option. Error messages of the
  factory arguments harmonized; the refusal of the adaptive tolerance by
  the fixed point solver says how to change the method.
- Chebyshev smoother: orders from 1 to 5 (MFEM aborts otherwise).
- Tests: the relative tolerances of the iterations of the Newton solver and
  of NewtonK0 are computed again by the test from the iterations
  information (absolute convergence criterion), and the norm of the
  residual of each linear solve must be lower than the norm of the residual
  of the non linear problem; three iterations of the first choice with an
  active safeguard; error messages of the refusals. The ten mutations of
  the review (sign and value of the linear residual, frozen tolerance, no
  bound against oversolving, safeguard of the first choice) are detected.
  The counter of the resolutions by a destroyed linear solver, which could
  not count (a call of a destroyed solver crashes), is removed.
---
